1
00:01:41,155 --> 00:01:43,011
Just... just don't, man.

2
00:01:43,011 --> 00:01:44,696
Okay.

3
00:01:44,696 --> 00:01:46,766
So cute.

4
00:01:46,766 --> 00:01:50,920
Joy, come on. Stop teasing me.

5
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:53,856
Jim, I need your help.

6
00:01:53,856 --> 00:01:55,440
Anything.

7
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:59,984
I'm going live to expose the truth
about Weechana.

8
00:02:01,366 --> 00:02:04,540
The clip I put out earlier
only stirred things up.

9
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,315
It wasn't enough to actually bring him down.

10
00:02:07,315 --> 00:02:11,021
So I decided to show my face
and tell everyone the whole story.

11
00:02:11,021 --> 00:02:13,020
And I can be a key witness
in several other cases

12
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:16,160
the police don't even know about yet.

13
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,720
But... that'd be dangerous, no?

14
00:02:21,024 --> 00:02:25,806
I think if you go live,
he'll be able to figure out where you are.

15
00:02:25,806 --> 00:02:27,732
- That's our plan.
- What?

16
00:02:27,732 --> 00:02:29,115
If Eva goes live and exposes Weechana,

17
00:02:29,115 --> 00:02:31,454
he won't just sit back and do nothing.

18
00:02:31,454 --> 00:02:33,697
And if he tries anything,

19
00:02:33,697 --> 00:02:36,734
everyone watching will finally see him
for who he really is.

20
00:02:39,932 --> 00:02:41,774
Wow! Genius.

21
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,074
[Unknown]

22
00:02:57,233 --> 00:02:59,201
Hello.

23
00:02:59,201 --> 00:03:01,234
Hello, Pie.

24
00:03:01,234 --> 00:03:02,789
Eva?

25
00:03:05,142 --> 00:03:07,014
<i>Is Weechai with you?</i>

26
00:03:12,481 --> 00:03:13,835
Nope.

27
00:03:14,846 --> 00:03:17,006
I recognize that tone.

28
00:03:17,006 --> 00:03:20,057
You always lift your chin a little like that

29
00:03:20,057 --> 00:03:23,494
<i>when you're trying to bluff someone.</i>

30
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:29,044
Look, we've already come this far.

31
00:03:29,044 --> 00:03:33,300
Domino and Pat had talked about
keeping us safe,

32
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,654
they'd warn us
if something suspicious happened.

33
00:03:38,244 --> 00:03:43,140
<i>And that night at the party,
when Weechai slept with that woman,</i>

34
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,532
<i>I believe he was forced into it.</i>

35
00:03:45,532 --> 00:03:49,614
He had to do it because Weechana
was beating up the reporter in that video.

36
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:54,534
Why are you so sure about that?

37
00:03:55,212 --> 00:03:57,628
And why are you telling me about this?

38
00:03:57,628 --> 00:04:01,894
Domino saw everything and recorded it.

39
00:04:01,894 --> 00:04:05,174
And we both know what happened to her
after that.

40
00:04:06,068 --> 00:04:07,934
<i>Listen to me.</i>

41
00:04:07,934 --> 00:04:10,884
<i>The people in this family are ruthless.</i>

42
00:04:10,884 --> 00:04:16,041
My aunt was taken hostage
when Weechana proposed to me.

43
00:04:16,041 --> 00:04:18,526
And there's something else
you might not know.

44
00:04:18,526 --> 00:04:20,473
Ginny was secretly seeing Weechana.

45
00:04:20,473 --> 00:04:22,491
She tried to tell the press about it,

46
00:04:22,491 --> 00:04:24,404
and that's why she ended up
the way she did.

47
00:04:25,945 --> 00:04:29,044
It has nothing to do with me.

48
00:04:29,044 --> 00:04:31,689
- You don't have to...
- <i>Pie.</i>

49
00:04:31,689 --> 00:04:36,124
I'm just warning you,
like my friend asked me to.

50
00:04:36,124 --> 00:04:37,772
I just want to know...

51
00:04:37,772 --> 00:04:40,764
are you really okay with things
having to be this way?

52
00:04:40,764 --> 00:04:42,534
<i>And what if one day
Weechai has to take the blame</i>

53
00:04:42,534 --> 00:04:45,614
<i>for a murder Weechana committed?</i>

54
00:04:46,614 --> 00:04:48,556
<i>Why don't we help each other, Pie?</i>

55
00:04:48,556 --> 00:04:52,433
Let's not be the next ones
to end up in the news.

56
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:55,294
We can get out of this family safely.

57
00:05:12,006 --> 00:05:13,894
You really think that would work?

58
00:05:16,142 --> 00:05:18,468
I think it worked.

59
00:05:18,468 --> 00:05:21,742
From the way she sounded,
she seemed pretty shaken.

60
00:05:21,742 --> 00:05:25,574
Now we just have to wait
and see what she decides to do.

61
00:05:28,148 --> 00:05:29,949
So, what's next?

62
00:05:32,655 --> 00:05:34,604
You can call the person
who's going to break the story

63
00:05:34,604 --> 00:05:36,430
and tell them when you're going live.

64
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:40,889
Just give them a general location
so they don't get suspicious.

65
00:05:40,889 --> 00:05:43,890
We'll have Joy
help spread the word on our end,

66
00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:45,894
so we can get as many people watching
as possible.

67
00:05:57,441 --> 00:05:59,242
Excuse me, sir.

68
00:06:00,073 --> 00:06:02,638
There's news that Eva is going live.

69
00:06:02,638 --> 00:06:05,248
It came from the same page
that leaked the clip.

70
00:06:06,553 --> 00:06:07,972
You think it's strange?

71
00:06:07,972 --> 00:06:10,334
I agree. It looks strange to me.

72
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,793
So this is her counter-move?

73
00:06:14,793 --> 00:06:18,234
Using the live stream audience
as both a shield and witnesses?

74
00:06:20,028 --> 00:06:22,434
When? Where?

75
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,318
I think it should be
within four to five days,

76
00:06:25,318 --> 00:06:27,119
right before the election.

77
00:06:27,119 --> 00:06:28,941
Let me check with my sources first

78
00:06:28,941 --> 00:06:30,193
and see how reliable this information is.

79
00:06:30,193 --> 00:06:33,414
Don't worry about
whether the information is reliable.

80
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:37,654
If you find out where she is,
send someone to get her.

81
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:43,894
Even if it's a trap,
we can't let her go live.

82
00:06:44,702 --> 00:06:46,750
Take care of it.

83
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:48,551
Yes, sir.

84
00:07:03,368 --> 00:07:04,734
Hello, Dad.

85
00:07:04,734 --> 00:07:07,326
Could you send some men over?

86
00:07:07,326 --> 00:07:09,854
I heard Eva's planning to go live,

87
00:07:09,854 --> 00:07:14,700
so I want to keep her out of the way
until the vote count is over.

88
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:18,070
Sure, I'll take care of it.

89
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:20,734
Just don't get involved yourself, understand?

90
00:07:22,378 --> 00:07:24,179
Got it.

91
00:07:29,958 --> 00:07:31,759
What is it?

92
00:07:33,122 --> 00:07:35,399
Eva put out word that she's going live,

93
00:07:36,182 --> 00:07:37,498
so Weechana wants me

94
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:40,071
to send some men to grab her
and keep her out of the way.

95
00:07:40,071 --> 00:07:41,654
Why?

96
00:07:41,654 --> 00:07:43,692
Why do you have to keep her locked up again?

97
00:07:43,692 --> 00:07:45,953
As long as that woman is alive,

98
00:07:45,953 --> 00:07:48,998
Weechana is never going to
come to his senses.

99
00:07:50,046 --> 00:07:53,234
I'm telling you, have your men get rid of her
and be done with it.

100
00:07:54,281 --> 00:07:58,116
But people are watching us, Mom.

101
00:07:58,116 --> 00:08:00,534
But they don't have any evidence.

102
00:08:01,228 --> 00:08:03,948
No one can touch us, son.

103
00:08:05,142 --> 00:08:06,913
We've made it this far.

104
00:08:06,913 --> 00:08:11,038
When you bring her back,
make it look like an accident.

105
00:08:11,038 --> 00:08:13,774
A car crash or whatever.

106
00:08:13,774 --> 00:08:17,654
If your men can't handle it,
I'll have mine do it.

107
00:08:20,148 --> 00:08:23,094
I've killed someone onstage before,

108
00:08:23,924 --> 00:08:26,454
and no one could touch me.

109
00:08:27,492 --> 00:08:30,094
That stupid little bitch...

110
00:08:31,174 --> 00:08:33,414
with no pedigree.

111
00:08:35,964 --> 00:08:40,534
Your son's just days away from winning.

112
00:08:40,534 --> 00:08:43,854
Are you really going to risk it all
over some little food-stall girl?

113
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:47,134
I'll handle it myself, Mom.

114
00:08:48,302 --> 00:08:50,454
I know exactly what to do.

115
00:09:00,046 --> 00:09:01,847
Hello, Nok.

116
00:09:02,526 --> 00:09:05,284
<i>I really was threatened.</i>

117
00:09:05,284 --> 00:09:08,990
<i>Someone cornered me in the parking lot
and asked about your live stream.</i>

118
00:09:08,990 --> 00:09:10,991
How are you doing? Are you okay?

119
00:09:10,991 --> 00:09:14,569
<i>I'm okay. I told them exactly
what you wanted me to.</i>

120
00:09:14,569 --> 00:09:16,654
<i>All that's left is to tell them where.</i>

121
00:09:17,753 --> 00:09:20,014
Okay, thanks.

122
00:09:22,022 --> 00:09:25,654
Joy, we need to leak those photos right now.

123
00:09:27,030 --> 00:09:28,776
Weechana isn't stupid.

124
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:31,876
He'll be extra cautious before the vote.

125
00:09:31,876 --> 00:09:33,710
If we want him to come to us,

126
00:09:33,710 --> 00:09:35,934
we'll have to really push his buttons.

127
00:09:37,454 --> 00:09:39,042
Okay.

128
00:09:48,684 --> 00:09:49,713
I think this angle looks good.

129
00:09:49,713 --> 00:09:51,977
Can you move to the left just a little?

130
00:09:51,977 --> 00:09:54,772
Get closer, just a little.

131
00:09:54,772 --> 00:09:56,446
I don't think so. It looks staged.

132
00:09:56,446 --> 00:09:58,910
Okay, how about this?
Hold hands and spin around.

133
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:01,564
I will take photos from behind,
like candid shots.

134
00:10:01,564 --> 00:10:03,365
Stay right there.

135
00:10:04,044 --> 00:10:07,004
I want the photos to look candid.

136
00:10:07,004 --> 00:10:10,161
- You get it, right?
- Okay.

137
00:10:10,161 --> 00:10:11,506
So smart, my man.

138
00:10:11,506 --> 00:10:12,785
That's it. Keep posing.

139
00:10:12,785 --> 00:10:15,254
One... two... three.

140
00:10:23,126 --> 00:10:28,417
If this photo gets out,
there's no backing out of this anymore.

141
00:10:28,417 --> 00:10:32,558
Not with Weechana,
and definitely not with my fans.

142
00:10:32,558 --> 00:10:34,359
I'll try my best.

143
00:10:41,590 --> 00:10:43,654
Aw, this is so cute.

144
00:10:48,588 --> 00:10:50,780
Did you get it?

145
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:53,854
Oh, I'm sorry. Yeah, sure.

146
00:10:57,803 --> 00:11:00,214
Do you think this whole thing about Ginny
is true?

147
00:11:08,633 --> 00:11:10,694
It's possible.

148
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:13,873
Besides Ginny and the reporter,

149
00:11:13,873 --> 00:11:15,834
do you think there could be anyone else?

150
00:11:21,874 --> 00:11:25,089
Do you think it's possible that one day

151
00:11:25,089 --> 00:11:27,890
you might have to take the blame
for someone in your family?

152
00:11:35,478 --> 00:11:37,454
Let's run away.

153
00:11:38,342 --> 00:11:40,894
Now, while everyone's distracted.

154
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:44,834
I'm ready to run away with you.

155
00:11:46,932 --> 00:11:49,300
Why can't you think about yourself for once?

156
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,334
What about me? Don't you ever think about me?

157
00:11:53,697 --> 00:11:56,694
I need to think.

158
00:11:58,006 --> 00:12:00,654
They are my family.

159
00:12:00,654 --> 00:12:05,166
They're a bunch of assholes,
but they're still my family.

160
00:12:05,166 --> 00:12:07,737
But you have to choose.

161
00:12:07,737 --> 00:12:11,142
I'm not asking you to choose
between me and your family.

162
00:12:11,142 --> 00:12:12,774
I'm asking you to make a choice

163
00:12:12,774 --> 00:12:16,814
because I need to know
if you still love yourself enough.

164
00:12:25,934 --> 00:12:27,174
Shit!

165
00:12:27,174 --> 00:12:28,975
Fuck!

166
00:12:33,142 --> 00:12:35,372
<i>Did you see Eva's latest leaked photo?</i>

167
00:12:35,372 --> 00:12:37,388
<i>She was fully serving romance,</i>

168
00:12:37,388 --> 00:12:39,964
<i>kissing some guy against a mountain sunset.</i>

169
00:12:39,964 --> 00:12:42,513
<i>People are already making edits
with love songs and everything.</i>

170
00:12:42,513 --> 00:12:43,834
<i>And of course, the internet works fast,</i>

171
00:12:43,834 --> 00:12:46,521
<i>they zoomed in and figured out
it's that hot trainer</i>

172
00:12:46,521 --> 00:12:50,494
<i>who was seen running with her
a few months ago.</i>

173
00:13:03,452 --> 00:13:05,969
You've seen the photo, right?

174
00:13:05,969 --> 00:13:07,809
Where do you think it was taken?

175
00:13:07,809 --> 00:13:10,534
<i>I think it's Khao Yai, sir.</i>

176
00:13:10,534 --> 00:13:12,348
<i>At first, I thought it was Nakhon Nayok,</i>

177
00:13:12,348 --> 00:13:15,137
<i>but looking at it again,
I'm sure it's Khao Yai.</i>

178
00:13:15,137 --> 00:13:17,260
- Are you sure?
- <i>Yes, sir.</i>

179
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:19,596
<i>Your father has already sent people
to both locations,</i>

180
00:13:19,596 --> 00:13:21,397
<i>just to be safe, sir.</i>

181
00:13:22,513 --> 00:13:26,374
Then get the damn car ready
and come get me. Now.

182
00:14:05,414 --> 00:14:07,644
I don't think you should go.

183
00:14:07,644 --> 00:14:11,644
Tell my father's men to take care of Pun
once and for all.

184
00:14:11,644 --> 00:14:14,518
I'm going to get my girl back.

185
00:14:14,518 --> 00:14:17,041
And don't you fucking tell anyone at home
that I came here myself.

186
00:14:17,041 --> 00:14:18,396
You hear me?

187
00:14:18,396 --> 00:14:20,197
Yes, sir.

188
00:14:25,566 --> 00:14:29,065
We'll go live right here.
But if anything goes wrong,

189
00:14:29,065 --> 00:14:32,137
run back here and wait for me.

190
00:14:32,137 --> 00:14:34,057
There'll be an ATV parked up ahead.

191
00:14:34,057 --> 00:14:36,094
I've got everything ready.

192
00:14:36,937 --> 00:14:41,209
I don't think anything's gonna go wrong.

193
00:14:41,209 --> 00:14:44,486
Weechana wouldn't hurt me. I'm sure of it.

194
00:14:44,486 --> 00:14:46,780
I hope you're right.

195
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:48,854
But we can't let our guard down.

196
00:14:52,742 --> 00:14:56,969
And what if...
what if something does go wrong?

197
00:14:56,969 --> 00:14:58,934
What do you think will happen?

198
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:01,871
I don't know.

199
00:15:02,577 --> 00:15:04,460
But...

200
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:06,261
Do you trust me?

201
00:15:12,049 --> 00:15:13,498
I do.

202
00:15:14,886 --> 00:15:16,914
If I tell you to run,

203
00:15:18,518 --> 00:15:20,319
you run.

204
00:15:20,924 --> 00:15:22,725
Then wait for me here.

205
00:15:23,974 --> 00:15:25,340
Okay.

206
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:27,894
I won't let anything happen to you,

207
00:15:27,894 --> 00:15:29,695
I promise.

208
00:15:32,676 --> 00:15:34,574
And you have to be careful,

209
00:15:35,486 --> 00:15:37,287
promise me.

210
00:16:24,348 --> 00:16:26,149
Boat!

211
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,941
Why didn't you say something?

212
00:16:32,941 --> 00:16:34,665
I was hungry.

213
00:16:34,665 --> 00:16:37,876
The second I saw the news,
I knew I had to come help you.

214
00:16:37,876 --> 00:16:40,830
I asked my friend to take care of Aunt Da.

215
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:43,513
Yeah, his dad's a pretty powerful guy.

216
00:16:43,513 --> 00:16:46,454
But he is a good man.

217
00:16:46,454 --> 00:16:49,278
As soon as I found a ride,
I came straight here.

218
00:16:49,278 --> 00:16:51,118
I kept asking people for directions
along the way.

219
00:16:51,118 --> 00:16:52,665
I hadn't even eaten,

220
00:16:52,665 --> 00:16:54,628
so I had to stop and grab some grilled pork
and sticky rice.

221
00:16:54,628 --> 00:16:57,646
I was literally stuffing my face,
my mouth full of sticky rice.

222
00:16:57,646 --> 00:16:59,257
When the lights suddenly went out,

223
00:16:59,257 --> 00:17:01,113
I started knocking on the door
to get your attention.

224
00:17:01,113 --> 00:17:03,793
You called that knocking?
It was loud as hell!

225
00:17:03,793 --> 00:17:05,628
What?

226
00:17:05,628 --> 00:17:07,854
I was scared you wouldn't let me in, man.

227
00:17:09,372 --> 00:17:11,505
Why didn't you call?

228
00:17:11,505 --> 00:17:13,564
No one's answering.

229
00:17:13,564 --> 00:17:15,374
The line's busy.

230
00:17:16,225 --> 00:17:20,834
Oh, we were on the phone all day today,
planning everything.

231
00:17:21,654 --> 00:17:23,294
I'm glad you're here.

232
00:17:23,294 --> 00:17:24,615
Right.

233
00:17:25,484 --> 00:17:29,873
Tell me about your plan.

234
00:17:29,873 --> 00:17:34,505
Why would you suddenly say
that Eva had to go live?

235
00:17:34,505 --> 00:17:38,134
And that leaked photo that...

236
00:17:40,812 --> 00:17:43,329
Is this for real, or is this all an act?

237
00:17:43,329 --> 00:17:44,829
It's real.

238
00:17:48,694 --> 00:17:50,495
You should listen to the plan first.

239
00:17:52,857 --> 00:17:55,454
- Do you want to hear it?
- Sure, okay.

240
00:18:04,110 --> 00:18:05,534
So you're planning to go live

241
00:18:05,534 --> 00:18:08,440
and provoke Weechana into doing
something messed up in front of everyone,

242
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:10,680
and make him completely lose it.

243
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,016
Did I say it right?

244
00:18:13,454 --> 00:18:16,070
So you put the word out
that you were going live,

245
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:18,326
then leaked a photo
with just enough clues to your location

246
00:18:18,326 --> 00:18:19,964
to make it look accidental.

247
00:18:19,964 --> 00:18:23,974
That way, Weechana would definitely
come looking for you.

248
00:18:24,695 --> 00:18:25,888
Yeah.

249
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,228
I get all that, man.

250
00:18:29,228 --> 00:18:31,142
But...

251
00:18:31,142 --> 00:18:33,921
why the hell did you have to let him
take Eva too?

252
00:18:33,921 --> 00:18:38,054
So the police would have grounds
to search Chaichana's house.

253
00:18:39,292 --> 00:18:42,334
Aren't you scared, Eva?

254
00:18:43,342 --> 00:18:45,233
There'll definitely be a huge crowd tomorrow.

255
00:18:45,233 --> 00:18:46,943
Joy already put the word out,

256
00:18:46,943 --> 00:18:50,446
so there should be plenty of people
filming on their phones.

257
00:18:50,446 --> 00:18:53,508
I don't think anything too serious
is going to happen.

258
00:18:53,508 --> 00:18:57,294
Besides, the election is
just around the corner.

259
00:18:58,478 --> 00:19:00,484
We've already spoken to Ekachai.

260
00:19:00,484 --> 00:19:03,172
If Weechana or anyone else abducts Eva,

261
00:19:03,172 --> 00:19:06,780
the police will immediately have grounds
to search Chaichana's house.

262
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:08,996
Yes. We have to expose him

263
00:19:08,996 --> 00:19:12,454
at a time when he needs to
keep his image as clean as possible.

264
00:19:14,505 --> 00:19:17,833
I think this plan is great, let's do this.

265
00:19:18,486 --> 00:19:21,614
If you need me to do anything else,
just let me know, okay?

266
00:19:21,614 --> 00:19:22,990
Sure.

267
00:19:25,654 --> 00:19:28,574
You're quite something, man.

268
00:19:38,334 --> 00:19:40,105
Try to get some sleep.

269
00:19:40,105 --> 00:19:41,628
Okay?

270
00:19:44,614 --> 00:19:46,977
Whatever happens,

271
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:52,230
I swear I won't let anything happen to you.

272
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:55,454
I'll do whatever it takes to protect you.

273
00:19:57,542 --> 00:19:59,916
Promise me...

274
00:19:59,916 --> 00:20:02,694
that you'll be safe, my tutor.

275
00:20:04,034 --> 00:20:05,835
I promise.

276
00:20:27,761 --> 00:20:29,562
Are you sure?

277
00:20:31,334 --> 00:20:32,762
About what?

278
00:20:34,116 --> 00:20:36,294
About you dating her.

279
00:20:38,462 --> 00:20:42,934
People online are brutal.
You know that, right?

280
00:20:43,844 --> 00:20:49,054
You're already getting dragged
for being the other guy

281
00:20:49,054 --> 00:20:52,334
who stole the fiancée of
one of the most respected men in the country.

282
00:20:54,374 --> 00:20:56,630
And now they're digging up
everything about you,

283
00:20:56,630 --> 00:21:00,086
where you live, your family,
your parents, all of it.

284
00:21:00,086 --> 00:21:02,014
Yeah, I know.

285
00:21:02,790 --> 00:21:04,591
But...

286
00:21:05,422 --> 00:21:07,223
I love her.

287
00:21:14,950 --> 00:21:17,334
If everything works out the way we planned,

288
00:21:18,252 --> 00:21:24,326
you're still gonna have to deal with
all those assholes online who...

289
00:21:24,326 --> 00:21:27,380
I don't even know
what's gonna happen after that.

290
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:29,181
But...

291
00:21:30,532 --> 00:21:32,654
what if it doesn't go that way?

292
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,774
But you could die, man.

293
00:21:38,168 --> 00:21:40,067
Same goes for you.

294
00:21:40,067 --> 00:21:42,131
You're helping me,

295
00:21:42,131 --> 00:21:44,054
so you could get dragged into this too.

296
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,694
Well, I'm already in it.

297
00:21:51,726 --> 00:21:55,220
The thought has crossed my mind...

298
00:21:55,934 --> 00:21:58,305
that when all this is over,

299
00:21:58,305 --> 00:22:00,734
she might not want to stay with me.

300
00:22:02,758 --> 00:22:05,334
And I'd understand.

301
00:22:06,249 --> 00:22:08,050
She's famous and...

302
00:22:12,547 --> 00:22:14,105
I don't know.

303
00:22:15,828 --> 00:22:19,654
But I do know that if she chooses to stay,

304
00:22:20,918 --> 00:22:23,734
I'll do everything I can to be worthy of her.

305
00:22:27,231 --> 00:22:29,305
Come on, man.

306
00:22:29,305 --> 00:22:31,961
Let's just get through tomorrow first.

307
00:22:31,961 --> 00:22:34,958
Then we'll take it one day at a time, okay?

308
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:45,372
Good morning, sir.

309
00:22:45,372 --> 00:22:47,169
We're ready for the mission.

310
00:22:47,169 --> 00:22:51,537
Once she goes live, we'll trace the signal
and pinpoint her location.

311
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:55,196
I'd like you to confirm the order
one more time, sir.

312
00:22:55,196 --> 00:22:57,249
Take them all out.

313
00:22:57,249 --> 00:22:59,713
If you can make it look like an accident,
even better.

314
00:22:59,713 --> 00:23:01,514
Copy that, sir.

315
00:23:14,241 --> 00:23:16,436
Hi, everyone.

316
00:23:16,436 --> 00:23:19,385
<i>I'm sorry I've been away for so long.</i>

317
00:23:19,385 --> 00:23:20,817
<i>I've seen all your comments</i>

318
00:23:20,817 --> 00:23:23,225
<i>and all the love and support
you've sent my way.</i>

319
00:23:23,225 --> 00:23:24,969
Thank you so much.

320
00:23:24,969 --> 00:23:29,374
<i>Today, I'm finally ready to tell you all
the truth.</i>

321
00:23:29,374 --> 00:23:32,025
<i>- I am all ears.
- What really happens?</i>

322
00:23:32,025 --> 00:23:33,732
<i>Is she about to expose Weechana?</i>

323
00:23:33,732 --> 00:23:35,396
<i>Waiting for the tea.</i>

324
00:23:35,396 --> 00:23:37,782
<i>- #SaveEva.
- #LoveEva.</i>

325
00:23:37,782 --> 00:23:39,409
<i>#ProtectEva.</i>

326
00:23:39,409 --> 00:23:42,241
<i>- Make sure he faces the full consequences.
- Weechana, the Crooked MP.</i>

327
00:23:42,241 --> 00:23:44,614
<i>#AntiRuamThaiChanaParty.</i>

328
00:23:47,398 --> 00:23:49,614
Sir, we've got her signal.

329
00:23:51,782 --> 00:23:53,745
Jimmy Café?

330
00:23:53,745 --> 00:23:55,546
Let's go.

331
00:24:07,162 --> 00:24:10,854
There are four things I want to reveal today,

332
00:24:10,854 --> 00:24:14,673
and I have both witnesses and evidence
to back up every single one of them.

333
00:24:14,673 --> 00:24:16,334
Let's start with the first one.

334
00:24:16,334 --> 00:24:21,505
<i>My aunt was taken hostage
on the day Weechana proposed to me.</i>

335
00:24:21,505 --> 00:24:24,625
<i>I had no choice but to accept his proposal.</i>

336
00:24:24,625 --> 00:24:28,838
<i>Pun and his friend
have been helping me all along.</i>

337
00:24:28,838 --> 00:24:33,374
<i>They never kidnapped me.
That's a lie Weechana has been spreading.</i>

338
00:24:46,380 --> 00:24:48,974
Hey, can you drive faster?

339
00:24:50,384 --> 00:24:52,185
You're driving too slowly.

340
00:24:54,523 --> 00:24:56,490
We have 80,000 viewers already.

341
00:24:58,406 --> 00:24:59,916
The second one.

342
00:24:59,916 --> 00:25:03,132
Weechana's grandmother, Ms. Chanajit,

343
00:25:03,132 --> 00:25:04,684
<i>had me taken against my will
and threatened me.</i>

344
00:25:04,684 --> 00:25:07,630
<i>She forced me to help
with Weechana's election campaign,</i>

345
00:25:07,630 --> 00:25:11,854
<i>even though I had already
ended my relationship with him by then.</i>

346
00:25:12,836 --> 00:25:15,254
You will pay for this, bitch!

347
00:25:19,254 --> 00:25:20,962
Where are you?

348
00:25:20,962 --> 00:25:22,763
Hurry up.

349
00:25:27,716 --> 00:25:29,305
Hey!

350
00:25:29,305 --> 00:25:31,614
I told you to drive faster.

351
00:25:36,089 --> 00:25:37,212
Eva.

352
00:25:37,212 --> 00:25:38,799
Stall.

353
00:25:40,388 --> 00:25:43,589
As for Weechana's violent behavior,

354
00:25:43,589 --> 00:25:46,440
it wasn't AI-generated
like his party claimed.

355
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:49,356
That was the reality I had been living with
all along.

356
00:25:49,356 --> 00:25:53,553
Weechana would often show up at my gym
and cause a scene.

357
00:25:53,553 --> 00:25:57,028
Pun and Boat can both testify to that,

358
00:25:57,028 --> 00:26:00,202
<i>because they were threatened too.</i>

359
00:26:00,202 --> 00:26:02,054
100,000 viewers now.

360
00:26:18,419 --> 00:26:20,220
Fuck!

361
00:26:23,046 --> 00:26:26,534
Tell my father's men to go get her. Now.

362
00:26:26,534 --> 00:26:28,132
But there are many people outside.

363
00:26:28,132 --> 00:26:29,961
If we storm in there and take her now,
I'm afraid...

364
00:26:29,961 --> 00:26:32,270
Just shoot her! Shoot her!

365
00:26:32,270 --> 00:26:34,265
Are you waiting for her to say my name too?

366
00:26:34,265 --> 00:26:35,414
Shoot her!

367
00:26:35,414 --> 00:26:38,014
Yes, ma'am.

368
00:26:43,364 --> 00:26:44,865
The third one.

369
00:26:44,865 --> 00:26:49,094
I'm fairly certain that
Weechana's younger brother, Weechai,

370
00:26:49,094 --> 00:26:50,725
<i>has been stirring up scandals</i>

371
00:26:50,725 --> 00:26:52,508
<i>to bury negative stories
about his brother all along.</i>

372
00:26:52,508 --> 00:26:53,873
<i>That incident happened on the same day</i>

373
00:26:53,873 --> 00:26:58,054
<i>Weechana assaulted a reporter
who was later found dead.</i>

374
00:27:10,601 --> 00:27:12,076
Go!

375
00:27:21,726 --> 00:27:23,527
What the hell is this?

376
00:27:24,834 --> 00:27:26,635
Get down!

377
00:27:34,644 --> 00:27:36,994
<i>- What is happening?
- Why are there so many people here?</i>

378
00:27:36,994 --> 00:27:38,841
<i>Did Weechana do this?</i>

379
00:27:38,841 --> 00:27:40,334
<i>Everyone gets possessive over what's theirs.</i>

380
00:27:40,334 --> 00:27:42,532
<i>Please, let Eva be safe.</i>

381
00:27:42,532 --> 00:27:43,964
You!

382
00:27:55,700 --> 00:27:57,501
Eva, let's go.

383
00:28:05,270 --> 00:28:07,654
Oh my gosh!

384
00:28:07,654 --> 00:28:09,985
Oh my gosh!

385
00:28:09,985 --> 00:28:12,609
My café is wrecked!

386
00:28:12,609 --> 00:28:14,984
Who's gonna pay for all this damage?

387
00:28:19,714 --> 00:28:21,240
Get lost!

388
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:22,630
Let's go.

389
00:28:26,054 --> 00:28:28,085
You son of a bitch!

390
00:28:28,085 --> 00:28:30,234
Who told you to shoot?

391
00:28:31,534 --> 00:28:33,335
Sir, you can't go.

392
00:28:35,494 --> 00:28:37,295
Who told him to shoot?

393
00:28:38,254 --> 00:28:40,334
- You should get back in the car.
- Asshole.

394
00:28:51,681 --> 00:28:53,281
Hey! Stop!

395
00:28:53,281 --> 00:28:55,082
Stop! Damn it!

396
00:29:05,132 --> 00:29:07,174
Aim for the wheels.

397
00:29:25,246 --> 00:29:26,938
Hey! Stop!

398
00:29:28,492 --> 00:29:30,024
Stop!

399
00:29:32,094 --> 00:29:33,494
Stop!

400
00:29:36,782 --> 00:29:39,084
Hey! Stop running.

401
00:29:40,583 --> 00:29:42,285
Don't shoot her.

402
00:29:42,285 --> 00:29:44,134
Don't shoot! Don't shoot her!

403
00:29:59,817 --> 00:30:01,169
Pun?

404
00:30:02,185 --> 00:30:03,986
Pun!

405
00:30:07,529 --> 00:30:09,015
Pun!

406
00:30:10,788 --> 00:30:12,294
Pun!

407
00:30:12,294 --> 00:30:15,534
Pun! Wake up! Please, you have to be okay!

408
00:30:15,534 --> 00:30:18,734
Pun, wake up!

409
00:30:18,734 --> 00:30:21,372
Pun! Please, you have to be okay!

410
00:30:21,372 --> 00:30:24,748
Wake up! Do you hear me?

411
00:30:24,748 --> 00:30:27,462
Wake up! Come on!

412
00:30:27,462 --> 00:30:29,334
Do you hear me? Please, wake up!

413
00:30:29,334 --> 00:30:31,617
Please be okay.

414
00:30:31,617 --> 00:30:33,260
- Pun!
- Get Eva.

415
00:30:33,260 --> 00:30:35,521
- You hear me?
- And you...

416
00:30:35,521 --> 00:30:36,854
You need to get rid of him.

417
00:30:36,854 --> 00:30:38,334
Pun! Wake up!

418
00:30:38,334 --> 00:30:40,260
Let me go! Pun!

419
00:30:40,260 --> 00:30:42,500
Let me go! Get away from me!

420
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:43,814
Pun!

421
00:30:43,814 --> 00:30:45,615
Eva.

422
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:52,280
- Bring her away.
- Pun!

423
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:55,731
Don't you dare do anything to him!

424
00:31:05,948 --> 00:31:08,054
You can cry all you want on the way back.

425
00:31:09,776 --> 00:31:11,694
He's as good as dead anyway.

426
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:17,033
Weechana, please?

427
00:31:17,033 --> 00:31:21,354
Can you tell your men to leave Pun alone?
Please, I'm begging you.

428
00:31:22,974 --> 00:31:24,894
I wish I could help,

429
00:31:25,785 --> 00:31:28,574
but those men don't work for me.

430
00:31:28,574 --> 00:31:30,614
They work for my dad.

431
00:31:31,700 --> 00:31:33,296
Sorry.

432
00:31:36,958 --> 00:31:41,014
Can you let Pun go, please?

433
00:31:41,014 --> 00:31:46,049
Please, I'm begging you. Let him go.

434
00:31:46,049 --> 00:31:49,830
- Boss, actually...
- Nobody is asking you anything.

435
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:52,678
- Shut up!
- But it's already gone viral.

436
00:31:52,678 --> 00:31:54,854
I think the party won't be happy with it.

437
00:31:59,740 --> 00:32:02,934
Where are you going to take Eva?

438
00:32:06,899 --> 00:32:08,367
Fuck!

439
00:32:17,233 --> 00:32:18,956
Hello, Weechai.

440
00:32:18,956 --> 00:32:20,854
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

441
00:32:21,664 --> 00:32:23,790
It has to be you.

442
00:32:23,790 --> 00:32:25,591
I have no one else.

443
00:32:40,478 --> 00:32:43,508
He's conscious again. Get him up.

444
00:32:43,508 --> 00:32:45,159
Come on.

445
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:49,767
Get up!

446
00:33:29,473 --> 00:33:31,617
Hey! Pull back!

447
00:33:31,617 --> 00:33:33,418
Follow them!

448
00:33:36,558 --> 00:33:38,094
Pun!

449
00:33:38,094 --> 00:33:40,046
Pun!

450
00:33:40,046 --> 00:33:42,961
- Boat!
- Pun!

451
00:33:42,961 --> 00:33:44,525
Jim.

452
00:33:46,782 --> 00:33:48,081
Be careful.

453
00:33:48,081 --> 00:33:50,854
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

454
00:33:52,017 --> 00:33:53,436
Where is Eva?

455
00:33:53,436 --> 00:33:55,520
Weechana took Eva.

456
00:33:55,520 --> 00:33:58,107
Okay... okay...

457
00:34:05,182 --> 00:34:07,881
- <i>Hello.</i>
- Weechana took Eva.

458
00:34:07,881 --> 00:34:10,916
Okay. I'll get the word to my men right away.

459
00:34:10,916 --> 00:34:12,724
And don't worry.

460
00:34:12,724 --> 00:34:15,299
We've got every route into Khao Yai covered.

461
00:34:18,942 --> 00:34:20,743
What's the matter?

462
00:34:23,612 --> 00:34:26,809
The local police caught up with them,
and there was a shootout.

463
00:34:26,809 --> 00:34:29,454
Our people are trying to pull some strings
to help.

464
00:34:30,686 --> 00:34:32,487
Damn it!

465
00:34:34,278 --> 00:34:37,021
You shouldn't have done it.

466
00:34:37,021 --> 00:34:40,342
What? Me again? What did I do this time?

467
00:34:40,342 --> 00:34:42,563
You yelled into the phone
and told them to shoot!

468
00:34:42,563 --> 00:34:44,275
What?

469
00:34:44,275 --> 00:34:46,617
Are you going to wait
until she exposes everything you've done?

470
00:34:46,617 --> 00:34:50,054
You're pathetic.
You can't even think for yourself.

471
00:34:50,729 --> 00:34:54,809
None of this would be a problem
if you hadn't crossed the line, Mom.

472
00:34:54,809 --> 00:34:56,713
And then Weechana had to show up there.

473
00:34:56,713 --> 00:34:58,434
What? Are you serious?

474
00:34:58,434 --> 00:35:01,934
Weechana went and grabbed Eva himself.

475
00:35:03,273 --> 00:35:08,274
What's gotten into him?
He's driving me insane!

476
00:35:08,274 --> 00:35:10,521
I'm the one who's going crazy here!

477
00:35:10,521 --> 00:35:13,713
Neither the mother nor the son
ever fucking listens to me.

478
00:35:13,713 --> 00:35:15,351
They both think they know everything!

479
00:35:16,163 --> 00:35:17,228
Ma'am?

480
00:35:17,228 --> 00:35:18,481
- What?
- What?

481
00:35:18,481 --> 00:35:22,614
Someone posted that a man
who looks like Weechana was at the scene.

482
00:35:30,494 --> 00:35:32,846
The bullet grazed you pretty badly.

483
00:35:32,846 --> 00:35:34,670
Take it easy for now.

484
00:35:34,670 --> 00:35:37,161
- You don't want the wound to open up again.
- Okay.

485
00:35:37,161 --> 00:35:39,814
- That's it.
- Thank you so much.

486
00:35:47,987 --> 00:35:50,228
<i>My source spotted the target vehicle.</i>

487
00:35:50,228 --> 00:35:51,907
<i>They're heading into Bangkok.</i>

488
00:35:51,907 --> 00:35:54,761
<i>I've already reached out to a contact
in the Highway Police.</i>

489
00:35:54,761 --> 00:35:57,035
<i>We won't lose Eva this time.</i>

490
00:35:57,035 --> 00:35:58,974
Got it.

491
00:35:58,974 --> 00:36:01,086
I'll head back to Bangkok tonight.

492
00:36:02,988 --> 00:36:04,989
Jim, I gotta use your car, man.

493
00:36:04,989 --> 00:36:06,129
Of course.

494
00:36:06,129 --> 00:36:08,300
Hold on.

495
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:10,332
You're not gonna rest?

496
00:36:10,332 --> 00:36:12,534
You're gonna drive.

497
00:36:13,249 --> 00:36:15,894
I'll pay for all the damages at your café.

498
00:36:16,913 --> 00:36:18,895
Go and save your girl.
